# BT Business — Paper Register, Not Tally

These rules apply to the **entire project** unless explicitly approved otherwise.

## Target user
Shopkeepers and wholesalers who **write everything in a notebook** today. **Zero accounting knowledge.** Must be **easier than Tally**.

## Golden rule
If a feature feels like **Tally or accounting software**, remove it or hide it from the user.
The app must always feel like **writing in a paper register**.

---

## 1. Simplicity First
Every screen stays simple. If a feature complicates the UI, redesign the feature — not the user flow.

- Max **2–3 taps** for common work
- **Minimum typing**
- No unnecessary dialogs, confusing workflows, or hidden important actions
- **5–6 fields max** per form

## 2. Hindi First
All user-visible text: **simple daily spoken Hindi**.

Examples: Party chuniye · Maal chuniye · Kitna mila · Kitna baaki · Paisa mila · Kharcha · Bikri · Kharid · Poora hisaab · Save karein · Edit karein · Delete karein

**Never expose in UI:** Invoice · Posting · Migration · Database · Repository · Engine · Service · Audit · Linked rows · Transaction · Recalculate · Sync · Journal · Voucher · Debit · Credit · HSN · GSTIN

Code may use accounting terms internally — **never expose to users**.

## 3. Voice First Workflow
Assume users may **speak instead of type**. Voice wherever practical. Typing optional. Every new feature considers voice first.

## 4. Auto-Creation Philosophy
During Sale/Purchase, if item does not exist: **auto-create inline**, continue entry, no blocking warnings, no forced detour to item master.

## 5. Everything Must Be Editable
Users can always edit: Sale · Purchase · Payment received · Payment given · Expense · Party · Item.

**History is never read-only.** Help users correct mistakes.

## 6. Dashboard Philosophy
Dashboard shows **calculated** info only — never manually editable. Totals computed from transactions (never stored). Auto-refresh after every change.

## 7. Consistent Design
Same spacing, typography, colors, buttons, cards, icons on every screen. No screen should look visually different.

## 8. Branding Rules
Always use **Bharat Traders** branding (`assets/images/bharat_traders_logo.png`).

- **Splash:** Bharat Traders logo (`SplashPage`, ~2s)
- **Header:** BT Business + logo beside title (`BtBusinessLogo`, 40×40, `BoxFit.contain`)
- Never stretch or distort logo; keep clean professional spacing

## 9. Developer Credit
Every **vertically scrollable page** ends with footer via `DeveloperFooter`:

```
Developed by
Mohd Anas Mansoori
```

Small · elegant · low emphasis · professional · consistent.

## 10. Performance First
Never sacrifice speed for animations. Fast response > fancy effects. Avoid unnecessary rebuilds, delays, heavy animations.

## 11. Future Development Rule
Before any new feature, ask: Can this be simpler? Reduce taps? Reduce typing? Work with voice? **If yes, implement the simpler solution.**

